From 969251f7c5531c74b5a42358a82c3992bfdd545f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: 1aeo <github@1aeo.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 01:49:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] hsdir: Serve one onion service directory request per
 circuit

C tor never sends two onion service directory requests on one circuit:
anonymized directory connections use ISO_STREAM (dirclient.c), so every
descriptor fetch and upload gets its own circuit. Arti also uses a fresh
circuit per HSDir attempt and per upload, and Onionbalance uploads
through C tor's HSPOST.

Relay operators report HSDirs receiving thousands of BEGIN_DIR per
second, at roughly 5 to 22 BEGIN_DIR per new circuit. Remember on the
or_circuit_t that it carried an onion service directory request. On a
repeat request, count the circuit (exactly once per circuit) in the DoS
heartbeat and as tor_relay_dos_total{type="hsdir_circ_reused"}, and
count every repeat request as {type="hsdir_req_reused"} alongside total
anonymous HS requests {type="hsdir_request_total"} on the MetricsPort.

Counting always happens so operators and authorities can measure the
effect first. Enforcement -- closing the circuit with RESOURCELIMIT --
is off by default: a binary with no consensus or torrc opinion only
observes, and never silently tears a circuit down. The new
HSDirOneRequestPerCircuit torrc option (AUTOBOOL, like
DoSStreamCreationEnabled) overrides the new hsdir_one_request_per_circ
consensus parameter, which in turn overrides the count-only default.

The rule is limited to onion service requests, which only arrive over
connection_dir_is_anonymous() connections. Relays without DirCache
fetch other documents over one-hop circuits that also pass that check,
and they legitimately share a circuit (ISO_SESSIONGRP). That is also
why this is not a cell-level BEGIN_DIR limit.

On its own this removes the free per-circuit multiplier used by the
current tooling. A lasting effect needs the known-previous-hop rule in
the previous commit; otherwise a one-hop circuit per request from a
self-generated relay identity is cheap. Do not backport this commit
without the previous one.

Part of 41339.
