diff --git a/doc/man/tor.1.txt b/doc/man/tor.1.txt
index 64da71a10e..5ba5549336 100644
--- a/doc/man/tor.1.txt
+++ b/doc/man/tor.1.txt
@@ -3150,6 +3150,21 @@ The following options are useful only for a exit relay.
 
 The following options are useful only for an onion service directory (HSDir).
 
+[[HSDirOneRequestPerCircuit]] **HSDirOneRequestPerCircuit** **0**|**1**|**auto**::
+
+    Tor and Arti make each onion service descriptor fetch and upload on its
+    own circuit, so a circuit that carries more than one is not a stock
+    client. If set to 1, an HSDir closes such a circuit (with reason
+    RESOURCELIMIT) on the second request; if 0, it only counts them. "auto"
+    means use the hsdir_one_request_per_circ consensus parameter, and only
+    count if the consensus is silent. This option thus overrides the
+    consensus, which overrides the default of counting only. The reuse is
+    counted (in the heartbeat and as
+    tor_relay_dos_total{type="hsdir_circ_reused"},
+    {type="hsdir_req_reused"}, and {type="hsdir_request_total"}) in every
+    case, so an operator or authority can measure the effect before enabling
+    enforcement. (Default: auto)
+
